# Color

Use color intentionally.

## Roles

Color should communicate:

- hierarchy
- interaction
- status
- emphasis
- brand
- meaning

## Palette

Prefer a restrained palette.

Do not introduce a new color when an existing semantic token works.

## Semantic states

Use consistent semantics for:

- success
- warning
- error
- information
- disabled
- selected
- active

## Contrast

Do not rely on color alone to communicate state.

Pair color with:

- text
- iconography
- shape
- position
- state

when necessary.

## Dark mode

When dark mode exists, design it intentionally.

Do not simply invert colors.

Consider:

- surface hierarchy
- text contrast
- borders
- shadows
- imagery
- semantic colors

## Gradients

Gradients require a purpose.

Do not use them as default decoration.